cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KasFlex, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "KasFlex: verified agentic energy management for greenhouse horticulture under electrical constraints"
abstract: >-
  KasFlex is a reproducible simulation testbed in which a language-model planner
  proposes hourly energy intent for a greenhouse energy hub, a deterministic
  safety checker verifies that intent against electrical, asset and crop limits,
  and a human approves or rejects it. It measures what verification and human
  oversight are worth, by running the same scenario with the checker enabled and
  disabled. KasFlex wraps existing validated components (GreenLight-Gym2 for
  greenhouse and crop physics, power-grid-model for network power flow) rather
  than reimplementing them.
type: software
